## API Rules

Everything is API First.

Never use Blade.

Never return HTML.

Always return JSON.

Response Format

Success

{
    "success": true,
    "message": "",
    "data": {}
}

Validation Error

{
    "success": false,
    "message": "Validation Failed",
    "errors": {}
}

Server Error

{
    "success": false,
    "message": "Unexpected Error"
}

Use:

GET

POST

PUT

PATCH

DELETE

Use correct HTTP Status Codes.

----------------------------------------------------------

## Coding Standards

Always

Use Dependency Injection

Use Interfaces

Use Constructor Injection

Use Typed Properties

Use Return Types

Use Enums

Use Form Requests

Use API Resources

Use Repository Pattern

Use Service Layer

Never

Duplicate Code

Hardcode Values

Use Static Helpers unnecessarily

Write Fat Controllers

Write Large Methods

----------------------------------------------------------

## Database Standards

Use MySQL.

Always create:

Migration

Model

Factory

Seeder

Policy

Resource

Request

Repository

Service

Controller

Use

Foreign Keys

Indexes

Soft Deletes where appropriate

UUID where necessary

Never modify database manually.

----------------------------------------------------------

## Authentication

Use Laravel Sanctum.

Prepare architecture for:

Email Verification

Forgot Password

Reset Password

Remember Login

2FA (Future)

Session Management

Device Management (Future)

----------------------------------------------------------

## Roles & Permissions

Use Spatie Laravel Permission.

Everything must be permission based.

Permission naming

users.view

users.create

users.update

users.delete

applications.view

applications.create

applications.update

support.manage

reports.export

Never hardcode permissions.

